  "claim_short": "Candidate full counterexample to Conjecture 1 of arXiv:2106.04116. The globally 1-Lipschitz smooth function F(x)=-sqrt(1+x^2) on R is strictly concave and nonconvex, while its Clarke subdifferential is the singleton {-x/sqrt(1+x^2)}. Because this derivative is injective, subdifferentials at distinct points are disjoint, so the conjectured intersection identity is vacuous off the diagonal and automatic on the...",
